NAME
    web-analyze - passive Chromium/CDP website evidence and Markdown analysis

SYNOPSIS
    web-analyze <http(s)-url> <analysis-path>

DESCRIPTION
    Launches a fresh headless Chromium session through the existing native-CDP
    web-analyze.lib.js recorder. The command waits for a rendered document,
    inventories controls/forms/headings and best-effort React runtime markers,
    scrolls the document and nested scroll containers, and records bounded
    rendered DOM states and viewport screenshots. It then stops Chromium,
    allowing the recorder's normal network/resource drain, and generates
    analytical Markdown documents from the acquired evidence.

    This is observation, not autonomous proof of every application behavior.
    The command does not click buttons, submit forms, authenticate, follow
    links, modify account state, bypass challenges or claim unseen states.
    An initial visit and scroll sweep cannot exhaust a dynamic React app.

OPERANDS
    http(s)-url       Required absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL to navigate.
    analysis-path     Parent folder for analysis runs. Created if missing.
                      Each invocation creates a unique private run-* folder;
                      pre-existing analyses are preserved unchanged.

OUTPUT
    Prints the absolute path to the generated README.md on stdout.
    Progress and diagnostics go to stderr.

    Inside each run-* folder:
      README.md        Analysis index, evidence counts, confidentiality notice
      DOM.md           Observed routes, headings, forms and interactive controls
      NETWORK.md       Request catalog (bounded summary), resource outcomes
      SCRIPTS.md       Compiled JS assets and best-effort React/Next evidence
      FLOWS.md         Mermaid diagram and table of observed scroll transitions
      LIMITATIONS.md   Coverage limits, missing resource outcomes and warnings
      states/          Per-state rendered HTML/text/controls in JSON, selected PNGs
      resources.jsonl  Complete CDP response capture index
      resources/       Decoded HTTP response body artifacts by content hash
      scripts.jsonl    Complete Debugger.scriptParsed source index
      scripts/         JavaScript source artifacts by content hash
      *.jsonl          Lifecycle, DOM, interaction, network and runtime events
      summary.json     Recording totals and incomplete-resource counters
      profile/         Dedicated Chromium browsing profile for this run

    The bounded exploration captures at most 29 states, with up to 1,200
    controls and 2 MB rendered HTML per state. Its final Markdown tables
    summarize a bounded prefix; the raw indexes retain all indexed outcomes.
    Resource capture is best effort. CDP cannot always retrieve bodies from
    redirects, active streams or evicted responses; inspect statuses instead
    of assuming complete acquisition.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires an initialized m environment (nonempty m_ROOT and m_LIB_DIR),
    Node.js >= 22 (native WebSocket) and chromium on effective PATH.
    From a clean shell invoke through: m web-analyze <url> <analysis-path>.
    Browser sandbox and TLS verification remain enabled; no Playwright needed.

SECURITY
    Private run directories and report/evidence files are created with
    restrictive permissions. Raw URLs, HTML, JS, response bodies, browser
    profile and screenshots may contain credentials, personal information
    or signed URLs. Do not commit or share output without review.
    CDP is bound to 127.0.0.1 with an ephemeral port and retains local
    debugger-level access during execution.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Completed and at least one rendered DOM state was observed.
    1   m environment is missing.
    2   Invalid/missing operands.
    3   Invalid URL.
    4   Unsupported URL scheme.
    5   Could not allocate a unique run directory.
    6   m library root unavailable.
    7   Existing web-analyze CDP recorder unavailable.
    8   Chromium capture initialization failed.
    9   Recorder finalization failed.
    10  Markdown report generation failed.
    11  No rendered DOM state observed (inspect partial evidence).
    12  Unexpected execution failure.

EXAMPLE
    m web-analyze https://example.org ./analysis

